{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3783","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3783","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3783\",\"parent_revision\":\"86c54bc1f950ab928192f772c6f0f93bb3200c35d2abddf09799adcc4a7aa1af\",\"root_revision\":\"86c54bc1f950ab928192f772c6f0f93bb3200c35d2abddf09799adcc4a7aa1af\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Docs\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-21\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nActive agent-facing guidance inconsistently duplicates standalone skilllint, linter, and formatter commands even though prek is the aggregate source of truth. These cached command lists create multiple authorities and can drift from the validation environment.\\n\\nRequired behavior:\\n- Keep one source of truth for validation guidance.\\n- Use `uv run prek run --files <changed-files>` as the single validation gate for changed files.\\n- Reserve direct tool invocation for capabilities that prek cannot expose, and state that exception where it applies.\\n- Treat the environment, including prek configuration and command help, as authoritative instead of duplicating cached command lists in agent-facing documents.\\n\\nImpact: agents currently encounter competing validation instructions, increasing maintenance cost and making completion depend on which guidance they follow.\\n\\nCompletion criterion: every active agent-facing validation path points to the single prek gate; duplicated standalone skilllint, linter, and formatter commands are removed unless a documented capability is unavailable through prek; one authoritative location defines the behavior.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - delegated backlog capture\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-21\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c0fa82e7c23814ee93c1883ad4a7250f0c5e4bd07cd3c57e41bbd4b57bc1f7e7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABWMlCiA\"}"}